          "kicker": "Women's test",
          "heading": "Ireland women look for strong response against Japan in Galway test",
          "body": "Ireland women seek a recovery in today's WXV Global Series fixture after last week’s 40-36 defeat to the USA. Head coach Scott Bemand has confirmed six changes, including a first start for Eilís Cahill in the front row and a return to the pack for Brittany Hogan. Following the late injury withdrawal of Aoife Wafer, the team will aim to improve their technical execution and arrest momentum shifts. Bemand noted the side is using this window to layer attacking prowess into their game."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales women lose 26-24 to USA in WXV",
