    "390": {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "URC club rugby",
          "heading": "Glasgow Warriors stun Munster as bench impact secures comeback bonus-point win",
          "body": "Glasgow Warriors opened their United Rugby Championship campaign with a 26-20 victory at Thomond Park, overturning a 10-point interval deficit through a dominant second-half surge. The Scottish side trailed for much of the contest, but tactical substitutions proved the difference, with Nathan McBeth and Seb Stephen inspiring an attacking shift. George Horne ultimately settled the result by scoring twice in the final quarter, sealing a vital bonus-point win as the hosts struggled to contain the visitors' late pressure."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales women lose 26-24 to USA in WXV",
