      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Women's test",
          "heading": "Wales women suffer narrow WXV defeat after Tafuna hat-trick for USA",
          "body": "The Wales women’s team suffered a frustrating 24-26 defeat against the USA in their WXV encounter at Cardiff Arms Park. Despite a spirited fightback that saw Keira Bevan, Kelsey Jones, Sisilia Tuipulotu, and Alex Callender cross for tries, the hosts were undone by individual errors and a dominant USA pack. Head coach Sean Lynn noted he saw \"grit\" and \"effort\" from his side, but admitted the team must learn to manage pressure and eliminate costly mistakes ahead of next month’s double-header against Japan."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
